WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.260
You know Margot Robbie and Ryan Gosling,&nbsp;
but what about all those other familiar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.880
faces in "Barbie?" Here's why all those&nbsp;
Barbieland residents look so familiar.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.500
Kate McKinnon is most recognizable as a former&nbsp;
cast member of "Saturday Night Live." Throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.340
her tenure on the show, she quickly became one&nbsp;
of the most iconic performers to ever grace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.320
the halls of 30 Rock. Some of McKinnon's "SNL"&nbsp;
highlights include characters like Ms. Rafferty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.340
a woman recounting her undesirable&nbsp;
encounters with aliens, and Sheila,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.280
a bar patron who gets hot and&nbsp;
heavy with her fellow barflies.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:36.120
"Hey, was your mother a beaver? Cuz damn - you&nbsp;
got a flat-tail furry face and smell like a lake."

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.080
Although McKinnon only recently left "Saturday&nbsp;
Night Live" in 2022, she'd already started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:48.300
steadily building a film career for herself prior&nbsp;
to leaving, with roles in the 2016 "Ghostbusters"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.680
reboot as well as comedies like "Rough Night,"&nbsp;
"The Spy Who Dumped Me," and "Yesterday."

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.880
Given her extensive comedy background, as&nbsp;
well as her penchant for playing strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.600
characters on "Saturday Night Live," she&nbsp;
was the perfect fit for Weird Barbie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.160
the outcast Barbie whom little girls play&nbsp;
with too hard. Speaking to Entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:08.640
Weekly on her visual inspiration for&nbsp;
Weird Barbie, McKinnon commented:

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.180
"I just pulled a bunch of pictures&nbsp;
off the internet. I think I typed in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.320
like, 'effed up doll.'"

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.460
In "Barbie," Simu Liu is one of the&nbsp;
more significant Kens in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:23.220
rivaling Ryan Gosling's Ken for Barbie's attention&nbsp;
and even engaging in an extravagant, '80s-themed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.540
dance battle during the film's climax. For&nbsp;
audiences who aren't aware of Liu's prior work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.620
they might have been surprised to see this Ken&nbsp;
perform numerous backflips throughout the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:36.120
which no other Ken can replicate. However,&nbsp;
this is all in a day's work for Liu.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:41.460
Prior to the mainstream success of "Barbie," Liu&nbsp;
was mostly known for appearing in the 2021 Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:46.500
Cinematic Universe film "Shang-Chi and the Legend&nbsp;
of the Ten Rings," playing the titular martial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.400
artist who is forced to confront his father,&nbsp;
the leader of a vast criminal organization.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:56.220
"Dad, please. Your family needs you."

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.600
Liu notably performed as many of his&nbsp;
own stunts as possible as Shang-Chi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.740
which was no easy feat to master for&nbsp;
the role. He told Entertainment Weekly:

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.380
"I want to sit here and tell you&nbsp;
that I was pretty good at martial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.100
arts before. […] But really, my martial&nbsp;
arts experience was like backflipping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.520
in my backyard when I was a teenager&nbsp;
and doing parkour with my friends."

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.260
Aside from his work in the world of Marvel,&nbsp;
Liu also gained notoriety for starring in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.820
the Canadian sitcom "Kim's Convenience"&nbsp;
and also appeared in the 2023 romantic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:28.620
drama "One True Loves" opposite Phillipa Soo.&nbsp;
However, Liu will likely look back on "Barbie"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.460
as a formative experience in his so-far&nbsp;
short but promising career in Hollywood.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:37.500
Issa Rae first gained everybody's attention&nbsp;
with her self-produced internet web series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.880
"The Mis-Adventures of Awkward Black Girl,"&nbsp;
which was later adapted into the successful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:47.520
HBO comedy "Insecure". Created by and starring&nbsp;
Rae, it follows a woman navigating social life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.000
romance, and contemporary life&nbsp;
for an African-American woman.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.180
"We are not about to be the Black&nbsp;
couple fighting in Rite-Aid."

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.840
The series was the recipient of&nbsp;
many Emmy nominations and launched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.860
Rae into the limelight as one of the most&nbsp;
talked-about young creative minds of the 2010s.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:07.920
"Insecure" concluded its run on HBO in 2021,&nbsp;
but Rae has remained busy ever since. In 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.360
she flexed her acting range with the romantic&nbsp;
drama "The Photograph" and the romantic comedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.680
"The Lovebirds." On the TV side of things,&nbsp;
Rae has also appeared in various sketches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.580
on HBO's "A Black Lady Sketch Show,"&nbsp;
which she also executive produces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:26.160
and hosted "Saturday Night Live" in 2020.&nbsp;
More recently, Rae lent her voice to 2023's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.120
"Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse"&nbsp;
as Jessica Drew — aka Spider-Woman.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.620
In "Barbie," Issa Rae plays President&nbsp;
Barbie, who, unlike Margot Robbie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:39.300
Stereotypical Barbie, becomes victim to the&nbsp;
Kens' brainwashing after Gosling's Ken takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.020
over Barbieland. On the film's themes&nbsp;
about womanhood, Rae told Girls United:

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:47.760
"It's really just up to you about how you want&nbsp;
to present and how you want people to see you."

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:53.100
America Ferrera has a unique role in "Barbie"&nbsp;
compared to most other cast members. Rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:57.600
than play a resident of Barbieland, Ferrera&nbsp;
plays Gloria, a hard-working mother employed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.340
as a secretary at Mattel whose existential crisis&nbsp;
results in her playing with her daughter's Barbie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:07.380
creating a dimensional rift that brings Margot&nbsp;
Robbie's Barbie into the real world. Ferrera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.440
also gets the privilege of delivering&nbsp;
perhaps the best monologue in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:15.000
ranting to the Barbies about the contradictory&nbsp;
expectations placed on women in the real world.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.260
Though some audiences may be delightfully&nbsp;
surprised by just how much Ferrera steals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:23.640
the show, true fans of the actress have known&nbsp;
her strengths for years. Her film debut was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:27.600
in 2002's "Real Women Have Curves,"&nbsp;
which has been regarded by many to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.740
one of the most influential films of the&nbsp;
2000s for its depiction of Latina women.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.240
"I'm not your baby anymore!"

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:39.120
Since then, Ferrera has starred in "The&nbsp;
Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.260
its sequel, "The Dry Land", and voices Astrid&nbsp;
in the "How to Train Your Dragon" franchise.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:48.780
Ferrera's breakthrough, however, came by starring&nbsp;
in the lead role in ABC's "Ugly Betty," centering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:53.640
on a girl who lacks style but gets employed at a&nbsp;
fashion magazine. After running for four seasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:58.740
before getting canceled in 2010, Ferrera then&nbsp;
starred and executive-produced in NBC's sitcom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:04.500
"Superstore" for six seasons as the floor manager&nbsp;
of a fictional department store called Cloud 9.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.980
In "Barbie," Alexandra Shipp plays&nbsp;
the Nobel Prize-winning Writer Barbie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:12.180
who is the first Barbie to be cured of the&nbsp;
brainwashing from the Kens thanks to Gloria's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:16.260
rant about how unfair the expectations put&nbsp;
on women are. According to the actress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:19.800
being a part of Barbie's world was&nbsp;
a dream come true, telling Out about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.820
how walking onto set for the first time&nbsp;
completely overwhelmed her. She said:

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:27.780
"It was so massive and up to scale that&nbsp;
the little girl in me started just crying."

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:32.160
That's high praise from Shipp, who has quite a&nbsp;
stacked resume for such a young up-and-comer in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.480
the world of film. She first gained recognition&nbsp;
portraying the singer Aaliyah in the 2014&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:42.060
Lifetime movie "Aaliyah: The Princess of R&amp;B,"&nbsp;
later making notable appearances in films like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:48.360
NWA biopic "Straight Outta Compton," LGBTQ+&nbsp;
rom-com "Love, Simon," and coming of age drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.920
"Dude" throughout the late 2010s. She also&nbsp;
entered the "X-Men" universe as the mutant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:58.140
Storm in the 2016 film "X-Men: Apocalypse,"&nbsp;
which she reprised in 2019's "Dark Phoenix."

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:03.120
Shipp later received recognition for&nbsp;
appearing in the 2021 musical biopic "tick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.860
tick... BOOM!," which stars Andrew Garfield&nbsp;
as playwright and composer Jonathan Larson.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:13.200
Emma Mackey's presence in "Barbie" alongside&nbsp;
Margot Robbie was a long time coming, considering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.740
how much the two actors were told they looked&nbsp;
like each other. In fact, there was meant to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:21.240
a joke referencing their similarity in the film,&nbsp;
but Robbie said in an interview with Buzzfeed:

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.800
"Once we got all dressed up as our Barbies, we&nbsp;
were kind of like, 'We don't look that similar,'"

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.680
However, Mackey still stands&nbsp;
out as Physicist Barbie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:31.680
yet another role in her steadily&nbsp;
increasing resume in Hollywood.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:36.060
Most audiences came to know Mackey through&nbsp;
her role as Maeve in the Netflix series "Sex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:40.500
Education." Mackey's performance in the show's&nbsp;
second season was notably critically acclaimed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:44.760
eventually leading to a rich career&nbsp;
in film, starting with the 2021 French&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:49.260
romance "Eiffel." Mackey also appeared&nbsp;
in the 2022 mystery "Death on the Nile,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:53.820
directed by Kenneth Branagh and based on&nbsp;
Agatha Christie's novel of the same name.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:59.640
Also in 2022, Mackey appeared in "Emily," a&nbsp;
biopic from Frances O'Connor starring Mackey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:04.380
as writer Emily Brontë, in a performance The New&nbsp;
York Times called "mercurial" and "mesmerizing."

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:11.040
"Charlotte says all the people in the village&nbsp;
call me the 'strange one'. Am I strange?"

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.700
The further acclaim Mackey received from&nbsp;
the film eventually led to her winning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:20.100
the BAFTA Rising Star Award at the British&nbsp;
Academy's 2023 award ceremony. So for those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.280
who enjoyed Mackey's role in "Barbie,"&nbsp;
get used to seeing her in the future.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.220
Kingsley Ben-Adir has had a short yet prosperous&nbsp;
career in Hollywood so far, though his experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:34.680
in performing Shakespearean theatre in the early&nbsp;
2010s has made him a tour de force of an actor. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:39.480
first rose to mainstream prominence in Seasons&nbsp;
Four and Five of the BBC period drama "Peaky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:44.400
Blinders," which was followed up by prominent&nbsp;
roles in series like "The OA," "High Fidelity,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:49.080
and "The Comey Rule," the latter of which saw&nbsp;
him appear as former President Barack Obama.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:52.380
In film, he appeared in "One Night&nbsp;
in Miami...," playing Malcolm X.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:58.440
"Louis X said that if I decide to leave the nation&nbsp;
of Islam, then I would be doing so on my own."

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.980
Most recently, Ben-Adir has completely&nbsp;
stolen the show in the latest Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:05.880
Cinematic Universe series "Secret&nbsp;
Invasion," where he stars as Gravik,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:09.540
the leader of a group of rebel Skrulls&nbsp;
who seek to take over planet Earth after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:13.740
growing tired of Nick Fury's failed promise to&nbsp;
find them a new home somewhere in the galaxy.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:18.360
However, Ben-Adir's role in "Barbie" is a huge&nbsp;
departure from his character in the Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:23.460
universe. Ben-Adir plays a Ken, and like all the&nbsp;
other Kens, he's desperate for the attention of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:27.840
Barbies, which coincides with the actor's own&nbsp;
desire to be in the film. As he told Variety:

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.740
"It's very rare that a script like that&nbsp;
comes along. So I was like, 'Whatever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:36.360
whoever is in it, I just want to be on set with&nbsp;
those guys and I want to be a part of it.'"

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:40.560
If Scott Evans looks recognizable, that may be&nbsp;
because you're mistaking him for his brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:43.800
actor Chris Evans, known for his&nbsp;
performances as Captain America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:48.000
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe, as well as&nbsp;
films like "Knives Out" and "The Gray Man."

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:50.700
"Ballsy."

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:55.140
Scott stars in "Barbie" as a Ken who fights&nbsp;
for the side of Simu Liu's Ken, while also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:59.280
having some obnoxious thoughts about finance that&nbsp;
one of the Barbies tricks him into telling her.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.380
Evans' career began on daytime television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:06.360
starring in the ABC soap opera "One Life&nbsp;
to Live" as Oliver Fish, a police officer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:11.160
whose LGBTQ+ storyline caused some on-set&nbsp;
controversy. Evans ended up playing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:15.480
role of Oliver for another two years before he&nbsp;
was eventually written out of the show in 2010.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:21.120
Since then, Evans has had many successful acting&nbsp;
roles, plus a cameo in 2014's "Playing It Cool"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.980
starring his brother Chris. In 2020, Evans&nbsp;
starred in the dramedy "Almost Love". However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:30.180
nothing in the actor's career so far has&nbsp;
stacked up to working with Gerwig. He told Out:

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:32.400
"I was in a state of panic the entire time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:36.420
just a huge sense of impostor syndrome,&nbsp;
knowing who else was a part of the movie."

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:41.460
Some who went to see "Barbie" may not have&nbsp;
recognized Ncuti Gatwa as Ken, but that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:46.080
will soon change. The Rwandan-Scottish actor&nbsp;
portrays the goateed Ken who fights alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:50.880
Ryan Gosling's Ken and Kingsley Ben-Adir's&nbsp;
Ken in the Battle of Kens. Like Ben-Adir,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:55.140
Gatwa got his start in Shakespearean&nbsp;
theatre before coming to wider acclaim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.140 --> 00:10:00.240
with his role in "Sex Education," which he stars&nbsp;
in alongside "Barbie" co-stars Emma Mackey and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:05.040
Connor Swindells. He also had an appearance in the&nbsp;
Netflix movie "The Last Letter From Your Lover".

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.880
Although his performance as Eric, the&nbsp;
best friend of Otis in "Sex Education",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:12.240
won Gatwa a BAFTA Scotland Award&nbsp;
for Best Actor in Television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:17.820
his breakthrough role is yet to come. In 2022,&nbsp;
it was announced that Gatwa would be succeeding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:21.960
Jodie Whittaker as the latest incarnation&nbsp;
of The Doctor in the iconic sci-fi series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:25.500
"Doctor Who." Although he was initially&nbsp;
announced to be the Fourteenth Doctor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:30.660
a surprise twist at the end of Whittaker's final&nbsp;
episode showed her Doctor transforming into David&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:35.520
Tennant's version of the character, with Gatwa&nbsp;
clarified to actually be the Fifteenth Doctor.

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:40.740
Gatwa won't make his debut as The Doctor until&nbsp;
a series of anniversary specials in 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:44.880
before the fourteenth season of&nbsp;
the sci-fi revival debuts in 2024.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:50.280
Hari Nef is a standout of the "Barbie" cast,&nbsp;
playing the role of Dr. Barbie, who also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:55.020
moonlights as a DJ for Barbie's Dreamhouse dance&nbsp;
party at the beginning of the movie. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:59.460
the role is far from her first breakthrough, as&nbsp;
Nef has had a groundbreaking career thus far as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:04.260
both an actress and model. After appearing&nbsp;
on the cover of a 2016 issue of Elle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:09.540
Nef made history as the first openly transgender&nbsp;
woman to appear on a mainstream British magazine.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:14.280
"I like to think that, if, like, my secrets&nbsp;
ever aired I'd be like 'Yeah? What about it?'"

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:19.320
As an actress, Nef first rose to prominence in&nbsp;
the Amazon Prime Video drama "Transparent," which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:23.580
centers on a family dealing with the revelation&nbsp;
that their patriarch, played by Jeffrey Tambor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:29.160
is a trans woman. Nef went on to star in other&nbsp;
popular shows like "You," "The Marvelous Mrs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:34.500
Maisel," and most recently in 2023, the&nbsp;
controversial HBO drama series "The Idol".

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:38.400
In the film world, Nef has had many notable&nbsp;
appearances since her breakthrough role in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:41.820
"Transparent." She has appeared&nbsp;
in 2018’s "Assassination Nation",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:45.240
the gaming comedy "1Up",&nbsp;
and Peacock's "Meet Cute."

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:50.880
Jamie Demetriou first gained notoriety in&nbsp;
the U.K. as a comedian, appearing in Phoebe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:54.960
Waller-Bridge's critically-acclaimed&nbsp;
2016 series "Fleabag" as "Bus Rodent."

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:59.580
Although Demetriou doesn't sport Bus Rodent's&nbsp;
horrid teeth in real life, it was a memorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:04.080
performance for many, given that the comedian&nbsp;
is now asked to reveal his teeth to strangers.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:08.280
Since his performance in "Fleabag,"&nbsp;
Demetriou has seen much success in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:13.680
both the U.K. and across the pond. In 2018, he&nbsp;
created, co-wrote, and starred in the sitcom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:18.600
"Stath Lets Flats," playing an incompetent&nbsp;
London letting agent. Demetriou's work in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:23.820
the show netted him a triple win at the BAFTAs&nbsp;
in 2020 for writing, performing, and producing.

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:29.700
His work has remained extensive since "Stath Lets&nbsp;
Flats" ended in 2021. He appeared in Season 1 of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:34.500
the Apple TV+ mystery "The Afterparty" as&nbsp;
the forgettable Walt, and also appeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:40.140
TBS's "Miracle Workers." In 2023, he wrote and&nbsp;
created a Netflix sketch comedy special titled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:44.880
"A Whole Lifetime with Jamie Demetriou." In&nbsp;
"Barbie," Demetriou plays second fiddle to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:50.220
Will Ferrell as the CFO of Mattel — a perfect&nbsp;
fit for Demetriou's awkward style of humor.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:55.140
Though she's still a teenager, Ariana Greenblatt&nbsp;
has built up an impressive resume. In "Barbie,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.140 --> 00:13:00.300
she impressed audiences as Sasha, the daughter&nbsp;
of America Ferrera's Gloria who is disenchanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:04.680
by the idea of Barbie and remains critical of&nbsp;
Margot Robbie's character until later having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:09.900
a change of heart after she sees Barbie slowly&nbsp;
become human. Before that, Greenblatt rose to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:14.640
prominence on the Disney Channel sitcom "Stuck in&nbsp;
the Middle" co-starring alongside Jenna Ortega.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:19.140
Greenblatt transitioned to film quickly after&nbsp;
debuting in "Stuck in the Middle," including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:24.360
appearances in "A Bad Moms Christmas," "Love and&nbsp;
Monsters," and "In the Heights." She even made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:29.400
her Marvel Cinematic Universe debut in 2018's&nbsp;
"Avengers: Infinity War," playing a younger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:33.900
version of Gamora during a flashback sequence&nbsp;
in which she's adopted by the Mad Titan, Thanos.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:40.260
"You're quite the fighter,&nbsp;
Gamora. Come…let me help you."

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:44.820
More recently, Greenblatt has appeared in&nbsp;
two sci-fi thrillers: "Awake," starring Gina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:51.000
Rodriguez, and 2023's "65" starring Adam Driver,&nbsp;
the latter of which finds the two sharing most of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:55.380
the screen time as the only humans on a strange,&nbsp;
remote planet that is actually prehistoric Earth.

